lavender: eMMC root device (rd=ufsroot0) through the SDHCI host

- bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c keeps its GPT lookup, BSD disk ufsroot0 and console log ring;
  the UFS transport is replaced by polled SDHCI commands on the eMMC host at 0x0c0c4000
  (sdhci-msm v5), data through one 64-bit ADMA2 descriptor per command (<= 60 KiB)
- card state as ABL left it; EXT_CSD read for size and cache, user area selected,
  CMD6 FLUSH_CACHE for DKIOCSYNCHRONIZE when the write cache is on
- 4 KiB blocks above the transport; GPT in 512-byte sectors, both copies fenced and watched
- the source change is made by xnu/src/mk_emmc.py from emmc_transport.c

